# 1. THE PLATFORM HAS THREE DISTINCT EXPERIENCES

The system is architected around three clearly separated areas:

```text
                                SaaS PLATFORM
                                      │
          ┌───────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────┐
          ↓                           ↓                           ↓
   MERCHANT ADMIN             MERCHANT STOREFRONT              IT ADMIN
(/store/[slug]/admin)          (/store/[slug])              (/platform)
```

### A. Merchant Admin (`/admin` or `/store/[slug]/admin`)
Used by each individual merchant/business owner and their authorized staff.
- Business control (Products, Orders, Customers, Inventory, Accounting, Expenses, Marketing, SEO, Settings).
- Database-driven Custom `AdminTheme` (Logo, Favicon, Primary Color, Sidebar Color, Light/Dark Mode, Density).
- Bilingual i18n (`বাংলা | English`) available in header.
- **NEVER exposes IT Admin links, other merchants, or tenant switchers.**

### B. Merchant Storefront (`/store/[slug]` or Custom Domain)
The public-facing e-commerce site for customers.
- Every merchant automatically receives a professional default storefront homepage upon store creation.
- Configuration-driven sections without separate hardcoded codebases for each merchant.
- Custom `StorefrontTheme` (separate from Admin Theme).
- 100% White-labeled on custom domains (`electromartbd.com`).

### C. Private IT Admin (`/platform`)
The platform owner's private control system.
- Dedicated platform homepage/dashboard (Stores, Subscriptions, Domains, System Health, MRR, Usage, Cloudinary Media Manager, Feature Flags, Audit Logs).
- Direct Cloudinary image/video upload with preview, progress, and secure URL DB saving.
- Controls merchants, subscriptions, custom domain verification, and Super Admin module feature flags (`StoreFeature`).
- Merchants must NEVER see or know of IT Admin.

---

# 2. MERCHANT CUSTOM DOMAINS + WHITE-LABELING

The system dynamically resolves incoming hostnames (`Host` header) to identify the correct tenant:

```text
Incoming Request (electromartbd.com)
      ↓
Host Resolver / Middleware
      ↓
Domain Lookup (StoreDomain)
      ↓
Active Tenant (ElectroMart BD)
      ↓
White-Labeled Storefront + Custom Domain SEO
```

1. **White-Label Requirement**: Customers visiting `electromartbd.com` see ONLY ElectroMart BD. No SaaS platform branding, tenant switchers, or internal IDs.
2. **Dynamic Sitemap**: `https://electromartbd.com/sitemap.xml` contains ONLY ElectroMart BD's indexable canonical URLs.
3. **Host-Aware Robots**: `https://electromartbd.com/robots.txt` points search engines directly to `https://electromartbd.com/sitemap.xml`.
4. **Canonical URL Strategy**: Canonical tags on custom domains output `https://electromartbd.com/products/...` (never platform subdomains).
5. **Domain Uniqueness**: The same domain can never be assigned to two different merchants.

---

# 3. CORE BUSINESS MODULES & ACCOUNTING

1. **Configurable Dashboard**: Metrics (Sales, Orders, Stock Alerts, COGS, Net Profit) computed dynamically server-side supporting Date Range filters (Today, Yesterday, 7 Days, 30 Days, Custom).
2. **Products & Dynamic Variants**: Attributes (Color, Size, Storage, RAM) with independent SKU, price, cost price, and stock.
3. **Inventory Management & Audit Log**: Immutable stock movement history (`InventoryLog`) recording `Who`, `What`, `When`, `Qty`, and `Reason` (`IN`, `OUT`, `ADJUSTMENT`, `DAMAGED`, `RETURNED`).
4. **Centralized Accounting Engine**:
   - Centralize authoritative revenue order status definition (e.g. `DELIVERED`, handling returns, cancellations, and partial returns safely).
   - $\text{Revenue} = \sum \text{Delivered Order Totals}$
   - $\text{COGS} = \sum (\text{Product Unit Cost} \times \text{Quantity})$
   - $\text{Gross Profit} = \text{Revenue} - \text{COGS}$
   - $\text{Net Profit} = \text{Gross Profit} - \text{Business Expenses}$
5. **Coupons & Marketing**: Percentage/fixed discounts, minimum order threshold, usage limits, and expiration dates validated server-side.
6. **Customer Reviews Moderation**: Moderate reviews (`PENDING`, `APPROVED`, `REJECTED`) per tenant.
7. **Cloudinary Media Manager & Upload Engine**: Multi-tenant isolated image/video upload, folder organization, preview, progress bar, and media library.
8. **Merchant Location & Map System**: Configurable business address, Google Maps location URL, Lat/Lng, and embed map on Storefront Contact section per tenant.
9. **Dynamic SEO Engine**: Entity SEO (Organization, WebSite, LocalBusiness, Product, Offer, BreadcrumbList) for search engine & AI discovery.

