# 121. ADVANCED SEO + AEO + GEO + AI DISCOVERABILITY MASTER RULE

The platform must be engineered for maximum legitimate discoverability across:
* Google Search
* Bing Search
* Google Discover where eligible
* AI-powered search engines
* Answer engines
* Generative search systems
* Local search
* Shopping/product search
* Voice search
* Mobile search

The objective is NOT to manipulate rankings.
The objective is to make every legitimate page, product, store, category, service, brand, location, question, and piece of useful content:
**Crawlable → Understandable → Indexable → Relevant → Trustworthy → Searchable → Citeable**

Never promise guaranteed #1 ranking.
Never use black-hat SEO.
Never create spam pages simply to capture keywords.

---

# 122. EVERY PAGE MUST HAVE A SEARCH PURPOSE

Every indexable page must answer a real search intent.
Before creating or indexing a page, determine:
```text
Primary Entity
Primary Search Intent
Primary Keyword/Topic
Secondary Topics
User Questions
Relevant Products
Relevant Categories
Relevant Store
Relevant Location
Internal Links
Structured Data
```
Do not create meaningless pages only for SEO.

---

# 123. PAGE-LEVEL SEO ENGINE

SEO must be generated dynamically for every eligible page:
```text
Title
Meta Description
Canonical URL
Robots
Open Graph
Twitter/X metadata
H1
Breadcrumbs
JSON-LD
Internal Links
Image Alt Text
Image Metadata
Sitemap inclusion
Indexability status
```
Never use one global title or description for thousands of pages.

---

# 124. PRODUCT-LEVEL SEO

Every product must be independently optimized with unique Product Name, Slug, SEO Title, Meta Description, H1, Description, Short Description, Image Alt Text, Canonical, Product Schema, Offer Schema, SKU, Availability, Price, Category relationship, and Breadcrumbs. Store Admin can override generated SEO fields manually.

---

# 125. DUPLICATE CONTENT PROTECTION

Prevent duplicate or near-duplicate pages caused by:
- Query parameters
- Multiple URL patterns
- Product variants
- Pagination
- Sorting
- Filtering
- Duplicate slugs
- Trailing slashes
- HTTP/HTTPS variations
- www/non-www variations
- Platform URL vs Custom Domain URL

The system must maintain one authoritative canonical URL for every indexable entity.

For example:
Platform URL:
`https://platform.example.com/store/electromart/products/iphone-15`

Custom Domain:
`https://electromartbd.com/products/iphone-15`

When a merchant has an active custom domain, the custom-domain URL must be treated as the storefront's authoritative canonical URL where appropriate.

Never allow multiple URLs to compete as separate versions of the same indexable page.

Use:
- Canonical URLs
- Redirects where appropriate
- URL normalization
- Noindex where appropriate
- Sitemap exclusion
- Consistent internal linking

Product variants must not automatically create duplicate indexable product pages unless they contain genuinely unique, useful content and have a legitimate search purpose.

Tenant A's canonical URLs, metadata, sitemap, and indexability rules must never affect Tenant B.

All canonical URLs must be generated dynamically from the verified tenant/domain context.

Never hardcode a merchant's domain, slug, or canonical URL.

---

# 126. CUSTOM DOMAIN HOMEPAGE INDEXING

Every active merchant with a verified custom domain must have an independently indexable storefront homepage.

Example:
Merchant: ElectroMart BD
Verified Domain: `https://electromartbd.com`
Homepage: `https://electromartbd.com/`

The homepage must:
- Render only that merchant's storefront
- Have merchant-specific title and meta description
- Have merchant-specific canonical URL
- Have appropriate Organization/LocalBusiness/WebSite structured data
- Be included in that merchant's sitemap when indexable
- Have correct robots directives
- Use the custom domain as the authoritative URL
- Contain accurate merchant identity information

The platform must never expose another merchant's homepage, metadata, sitemap, canonical URL, products, or structured data through this domain.

Search engines must be able to independently crawl and index each verified merchant domain.

Do not guarantee ranking position. The system only provides technically sound, legitimate SEO foundations.

